<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59820" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέξ</span></b> , ἡ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρεκός</span>, a long-legged bird, perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>corn-crake, Rallus crex</i>, or
				<i>ruff, Machetes pugnax</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούτους</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθους</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἐτύκιζον αἱ κρέκες τοῖς ῥύγχεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1138
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				695a22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				4.5
			</span></i>; sacred to Athena, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				3.5
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἶβις] μέγαθος ὅσον κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.76
				</span></i>
			; a name of ill omen to the newly-married, <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				4
			</span></i>: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δισάρπαγος κρέξ</span>, of
			Helen, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				513
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>noisy braggart</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				423
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>hair</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>: acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέκαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1528.18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
